      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we return false if `n \u0026 0b11111` is not zero, then I think we can simplify the code like:\n```\nbool IsFftInputSizeValid(size_t n) {\n    if (n \u003d\u003d 0 || n \u0026 0b11111)\n        return false;\n\n    for (const int factor : {3, 5})\n        while (n % factor \u003d\u003d 0)\n            n /\u003d factor;\n\n    return n \u003d\u003d 1;\n}\n```\n\nAlso if the input param `n` is known at compile time, we can make the entire method constexpr: `constexpr bool IsFftInputSizeValid(size_t n)`.",
